k;\n   258→            }\n   259→\n   260→            .section {\n   261→                margin-bottom: 20px;\n   262→            }\n   263→        }\n   264→    </style>\n   265→</head>\n   266→<body>\n   267→    <div class=\"container\">\n   268→        <header>\n   269→            <div class=\"header-content\">\n   270→                <div class=\"header-title\">🤖 Agentic Coding Research Report</div>\n   271→                <div class=\"header-date\">2026-06-25</div>\n   272→            </div>\n   273→        </header>\n   274→\n   275→        <main class=\"main-content\">\n   276→            <div class=\"three-column-layout\">\n   277→                <!-- New Products Section -->\n   278→                <section class=\"new-products\">\n   279→                    <div class=\"section\">\n   280→                        <h2 class=\"section-header\">🆕 New Products (1)</h2>\n   281→\n   282→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   283→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   284→                                <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/vexi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">VEXI</a>\n   285→                            </div>\n   286→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   287→                                Open-source AI coding agent built for developers who prefer the terminal. Bring your own API keys, connect OpenAI, Anthropic, and other providers, and accelerate coding, debugging, refactoring, and automation through a lightweight, multilingual, privacy-friendly CLI.\n   288→                            </div>\n   289→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   290→                                <span class=\"source\">📍 Product Hunt</span>\n   291→                                <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   292→                                <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-06-15</span>\n   293→                            </div>\n   294→                            <div class=\"community-quote\">\n   295→                                \"Open-source terminal-first agents are where a lot of real developer workflow will shake out. BYOK + provider flexibility is a good default.\"\n   296→                                <span class=\"quote-source\">— Community Feedback</span>\n   297→                            </div>\n   298→                            <div class=\"community-quote\">\n   299→                                \"What does VEXI do to keep long-running refactors inspectable before changes hit the filesystem?\"\n   300→                                <span class=\"quote-source\">— Community Question</span>\n   301→                            </div>\n   302→                        </div>\n   303→                    </div>\n   304→                </section>\n   305→\n   306→                <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n   307→                <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   308→                    <div class=\"section\">\n   309→                        <h2 class=\"section-header\">📋 Whitelist Updates (8)</h2>\n   310→\n   311→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   312→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   313→                                <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex CLI 0.142.0 Released</a>\n   314→                            </div>\n   315→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   316→                                Enhanced /usage command for rate-limit reset credits, improved /plugins organization with curated catalogs, configurable rollout token budgets, indexed web-search mode, and scheduled UTC time reminders. Major improvements to Linux TUI rendering, exec-server resilience, and plugin loading.\n   317→                            </div>\n   318→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   319→                                <span class=\"update-type release\">📦 Release</span>\n   320→                                <span class=\"source\">🏷️ Codex CLI</span>\n   321→                                <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-06-22</span>\n   322→                            </div>\n   323→                        </div>\n   324→\n   325→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   326→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   327→                                <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex App 26.616 with Record & Replay Feature</a>\n   328→                            </div>\n   329→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   330→                                New Record & Replay feature on macOS that turns demonstrated workflows into reusable skills. Added bulk actions to automation run history, thread handoff between local and remote hosts, and performance improvements including 2x faster Browser Use through CDP optimizations.\n   331→                            </div>\n   332→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   333→                                <span class=\"update-type feature\">✨ Feature</span>\n   334→                                <span class=\"source\">🏷️ Codex CLI</span>\n   335→                                <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-06-18</span>\n   336→                            </div>\n   337→                            <div class=\"community-quote\">\n   338→                                \"Record & Replay lets you demonstrate a workflow on your Mac and turn it into a reusable skill\"\n   339→                                <span class=\"quote-source\">— OpenAI Developers Documentation</span>\n   340→                            </div>\n   341→                        </div>\n   342→\n   343→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   344→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   345→                                <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex App Features Available in EEA, UK, and Switzerland</a>\n   346→                            </div>\n   347→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   348→                                Codex app capabilities expanded to European Economic Area, UK, and Switzerland including Computer Use on macOS and Windows, Codex Chrome extension for background tab work, Memories for preferences and workflows, and Chronicle as opt-in research preview for Pro subscribers.\n   349→                            </div>\n   350→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   351→                                <span class=\"update-type announcement\">🌎 Announcement</span>\n   352→                                <span class=\"source\">🏷️ Codex CLI</span>\n   353→                                <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-06-16</span>\n   354→                            </div>\n   355→                        </div>\n   356→\n   357→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   358→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   359→                                <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT for iOS 1.2026.167 Update</a>\n   360→                            </div>\n   361→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   362→                                Added per-host personality settings (Friendly and Pragmatic), goal editing in composer, forked conversation links, improved side chat visibility, composer autocomplete, progress visibility for subagents, and fixed long thread loading issues.\n   363→                            </div>\n   364→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   365→                                <span class=\"update-type feature\">✨ Feature</span>\n   366→                                <span class=\"source\">🏷️ Codex CLI</span>\n   367→                                <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-06-22</span>\n   368→                            </div>\n   369→                        </div>\n   370→\n   371→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   372→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   373→                                <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-06-04-github-copilot-in-visual-studio-may-update/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GitHub Copilot in Visual Studio — May Update</a>\n   374→                            </div>\n   375→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   376→                                June 2026 brought sharper tooling for planning, reviewing, and managing work with GitHub Copilot in Visual Studio 2026. New Plan agent lets you collaborate on implementation plans before coding, Skills panel for managing agent skills, multi-file summary diff for Copilot changes, and context window usage management.\n   377→                            </div>\n   378→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   379→                                <span class=\"update-type feature\">✨ Feature</span>\n   380→                                <span class=\"source\">🏷️ GitHub Copilot</span>\n   381→                                <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-06-04</span>\n   382→                            </div>\n   383→                            <div class=\"community-quote\">\n   384→                                \"Copilot is no longer a code suggestion tool. In 2026, GitHub Copilot in agent mode reads a GitHub Issue, spins up dedicated branches, writes code, and runs tasks autonomously\"\n   385→                                <span class=\"quote-source\">— CVE Optibot Blog</span>\n   386→                            </div>\n   387→                        </div>\n   388→\n   389→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   390→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   391→                                <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gemini CLI: Surgical Code Edits (v0.43.0)</a>\n   392→                            </div>\n   393→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   394→                                Released v0.43.0 with surgical code edits that prefer the edit tool for speed and precision, session export/import for portability, and adaptive token estimation for better context management efficiency.\n   395→                            </div>\n   396→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   397→                                <span class=\"update-type feature\">✨ Feature</span>\n   398→                                <span class=\"source\">🏷️ Gemini CLI</span>\n   399→                                <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-22</span>\n   400→                            </div>\n   401→                        </div>\n   402→\n   403→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   404→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   405→                                <a href=\"https://www.continue.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Continue Acquisition by Cursor</a>\n   406→                            </div>\n   407→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   408→                                Continue.dev has been acquired by Cursor. The website displays a notice stating 'Continue has been acquired by Cursor' with a commitment to ensuring developers are amplified, not automated. VS Code extension last updated on June 18-19, 2026.\n   409→                            </div>\n   410→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   411→                                <span class=\"update-type announcement\">🏢 Announcement</span>\n   412→                                <span class=\"source\">🏷️ Continue</span>\n   413→                                <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-06-18</span>\n   414→                            </div>\n   415→                            <div class=\"community-quote\">\n   416→                                \"Why the Cursor Acquisition Should Concern Everyone... I've been a Cursor user for a long time and today's acquisition news genuinely worries me\"\n   417→                                <span class=\"quote-source\">— Reddit - r/cursor</span>\n   418→                            </div>\n   419→                        </div>\n   420→\n   421→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   422→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   423→                                <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Devin: MCP Marketplace Expansion</a>\n   424→                            </div>\n   425→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   426→                                MCP Marketplace expansion with 48+ new engineering connectors now available, including integrations with Miro, Mixpanel, Honeycomb, Postman, monday.com, Klaviyo, and many others.\n   427→                            </div>\n   428→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   429→                                <span class=\"update-type feature\">✨ Feature</span>\n   430→                                <span class=\"source\">🏷️ Devin</span>\n   431→                                <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-06-11</span>\n   432→                            </div>\n   433→                        </div>\n   434→                    </div>\n   435→                </section>\n   436→\n   437→                <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   438→                <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   439→                    <div class=\"section\">\n   440→                        <h2 class=\"section-header\">💡 Technical Insights (0)</h2>\n   441→              